{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world","id":1018992,"title":"How does the Abrahamic Faiths have power in the Scion World?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-18T19:04:29-08:00","id":1018992,"title":"How does the Abrahamic Faiths have power in the Scion World?","content":"Now we've already learned that there will not be any Judaeo / Christian / Muslim type pantheon in the new Scion. Now the question is in a world where Gods are real (along with magic, mythological creatures, Titanspawn etc...) then how could have these religions survived to be the largest in the world? How could have these faiths almost eliminate the worship of a number of different paganistic faiths? Only the Japanese, Indian and Chinese Pantheons seems to have a large group of worship in the modern day while most other pagan religions have been relegated to small fringe groups of worshipers. First of all, if the Abrahamic faiths give no power then they would have not been able to become so dominant as the Pagan gods and servitors give REAL power, not empty promises. So the only way I can see Scion working is that A. It is an alternate modern time where the Pagan religions are still widely worshiped worldwide (Aka Think Percy Jackson) or B. The world is much like our own thus the Abrahamic faiths despite having NO POWER WHATSOEVER became the world's most dominant religion. How will Scion address this inconsistency?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2539-darkfire16","name":"Darkfire16","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T19:36:14-08:00","id":1019008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfire16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world#post1018992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now we've already learned that there will not be any Judaeo / Christian / Muslim type pantheon in the new Scion. Now the question is in a world where Gods are real (along with magic, mythological creatures, Titanspawn etc...) then how could have these religions survived to be the largest in the world? How could have these faiths almost eliminate the worship of a number of different paganistic faiths? Only the Japanese, Indian and Chinese Pantheons seems to have a large group of worship in the modern day while most other pagan religions have been relegated to small fringe groups of worshipers. First of all, if the Abrahamic faiths give no power then they would have not been able to become so dominant as the Pagan gods and servitors give REAL power, not empty promises. So the only way I can see Scion working is that A. It is an alternate modern time where the Pagan religions are still widely worshiped worldwide (Aka Think Percy Jackson) or B. The world is much like our own thus the Abrahamic faiths despite having NO POWER WHATSOEVER became the world's most dominant religion. How will Scion address this inconsistency?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well one of the big reasons could be that the Gods generally retreated from the mortal world for thousands of years and just left mortals to do their own thing? They might have popped back in once in a while to spawn the occasional hero, but they weren't making the same grand display of themselves that they used to. And most of the old religions were wiped out not because of willing conversion, but because &quot;heretics&quot; were forced to convert either through torture or the threat of death. And since the gods weren't answering their prayers anymore, most of these victims either lost faith in them, or they were killed by the Abrahamic zealots.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, just because the Abrahamic faiths doesn't give any power, doesn't mean the Titans don't. It was pretty obvious that the Titan of Light in 1st edition was supposed to be an allegory for the Abrahamic faiths by being the one and only being of worship, being too bright to look upon, and literally having angels serve him. Second edition might have another Titan who operates in the same fashion that was backing them throughout history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-18-2016, 11:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T19:59:08-08:00","id":1019020,"title":"","content":"Scion's history didn't happen in quite the same way as it did in the real world. Among other things, &quot;pagan&quot; faiths are more popular.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I don't think anyone said the Abrahamic faiths don't have any power. They're probably not <i>all-powerful</i>, but there'll be something there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T20:24:16-08:00","id":1019030,"title":"","content":"How many times is this thread going to pop up, god damn","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T20:36:19-08:00","id":1019032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1019030#post1019030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many times is this thread going to pop up, god damn</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably until the game about world mythologies and religions touches on the biggest ones still around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T21:19:55-08:00","id":1019040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1019032#post1019032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably until the game about world mythologies and religions touches on the biggest ones still around.</div> </div> </div> </div>But when the thread already exists, why do we have to keep making new ones or debating it in other threads?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T21:34:40-08:00","id":1019042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1019008#post1019008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, just because the Abrahamic faiths doesn't give any power, doesn't mean the Titans don't. It was pretty obvious that the Titan of Light in 1st edition was supposed to be an allegory for the Abrahamic faiths by being the one and only being of worship, being too bright to look upon, and literally having angels serve him. Second edition might have another Titan who operates in the same fashion that was backing them throughout history.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope we don't see an &quot;Aten 2.0&quot; route taken with 2e. That explanation, from what I remember personally, was only really satisfactory to folks with an axe to grind where the Abrahamic faiths were concerned (read: about half my regular tabletop group).<br /> <br /> It's been mentioned that Scion 2e in in a slightly-alternate universe, seeming to imply that the Abrahamic faiths never quite managed the wholesale overpowering of other religions. At a guess, that may mean that they're competitive with, but not superior to, the other religions. Akin, if you will, to one major auto manufacturer among many such.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","user":"yukikaze","date":". 12-19-2016, 12:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T21:44:24-08:00","id":1019050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1019040#post1019040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But when the thread already exists, why do we have to keep making new ones or debating it in other threads?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, I'm not making any of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yukikaze</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1019042#post1019042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hope we don't see an &quot;Aten 2.0&quot; route taken with 2e. That explanation, from what I remember personally, was only really satisfactory to folks with an axe to grind where the Abrahamic faiths were concerned (read: about half my regular tabletop group).<br /> <br /> It's been mentioned that Scion 2e in in a slightly-alternate universe, seeming to imply that the Abrahamic faiths never quite managed the wholesale overpowering of other religions. At a guess, that may mean that they're competitive with, but not superior to, the other religions. Akin, if you will, to one major auto manufacturer among many such.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't either, but I think the 2e fix is going to be &quot;El got a little big for his britches and has a couple different Mantles that make up one-God Pantheons.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T23:13:12-08:00","id":1019094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1019050#post1019050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't either, but I think the 2e fix is going to be &quot;El got a little big for his britches and has a couple different Mantles that make up one-God Pantheons.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm dubious that's going to be the answer myself.<br /> <br /> I have a hunch, though, that whatever the solution, the Abrahamics are not going to deny the existence of other gods. They'll be more henotheistic than exclusively monotheistic.<br /> <br /> One thing I came across I thought was interesting from Neall:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Scion's World is based on our world, albeit with subtle differences (like the small matter of all mythologies being true). The Abrahamic religions might be relatively unchanged, but the mythologies behind them would be significantly altered. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T23:17:28-08:00","id":1019098,"title":"","content":"Fate has a sense of humour? <br /> <br /> That makes sense doesnt it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T23:30:43-08:00","id":1019107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1019094#post1019094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm dubious that's going to be the answer myself.<br /> <br /> I have a hunch, though, that whatever the solution, the Abrahamics are not going to deny the existence of other gods. They'll be more henotheistic than exclusively monotheistic.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Either of those would be have more nuance and thoughtfulness than 1e's handling of the Abrahamic deity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T23:32:42-08:00","id":1019110,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yukikaze</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1019042#post1019042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope we don't see an &quot;Aten 2.0&quot; route taken with 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1019050#post1019050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't either, but I think the 2e fix is going to be &quot;El got a little big for his britches and has a couple different Mantles that make up one-God Pantheons.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Neal has already said that he likes that idea/explanation and that while Aten won't be solely responsible for the idea of monotheism, he will have played a large part in it. I think there was something said about him being responsible for exclusionary monotheism, though that confuses me since all monotheism is exlcusionary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T23:47:36-08:00","id":1019117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1019110#post1019110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neal has already said that he likes that idea/explanation and that while Aten won't be solely responsible for the idea of monotheism, he will have played a large part in it. I think there was something said about him being responsible for exclusionary monotheism, though that confuses me since all monotheism is exlcusionary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect Neall was referencing monolatry and henotheism there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T23:53:38-08:00","id":1019120,"title":"","content":"Riffing on the &quot;Fate can change the past through actions in the present&quot; - suppose that the Abrahamic deity[ies] managed in the past to change things [say around 2,000 years ago] so that the worship of the old Gods/Goddesses became mostly forgotten and suppressed [much like Amun worship in historical Egypt]. They have thus enjoyed a couple of millennia of unprecedented power, much like in the real world. Now, cue our current game world in Scion 2nd Edition, where the reactivation of Scions will once again prove the power and ability of the Old Gods, and show the masses of humanity that they <i>aren't </i>mere powerless myths. This causes Fate to change things once again so that the last 2,000 years of monotheism are suddenly ret-conned and suppressed to the point where they are [at best] equal to the rest of the faiths. Knowing that this would be the outcome of Scion creation was the prime reason that the Abrahamic faiths tried so hard to destroy the other worship all around the world in the first place. And so the &quot;All Myths Are True&quot;, the &quot;Abrahamic faiths still exist&quot;, the &quot;Aten didn't just pull the wool over your eyes&quot; and the &quot;Pantheistic faiths change the World&quot; would <i>all</i> be possible at once, and the direction of the world <i>from this point on </i>is up to the individual GMs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T03:28:38-08:00","id":1019148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1019094#post1019094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm dubious that's going to be the answer myself.<br /> <br /> I have a hunch, though, that whatever the solution, the Abrahamics are not going to deny the existence of other gods. They'll be more henotheistic than exclusively monotheistic.<br /> <br /> One thing I came across I thought was interesting from Neall:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fun fact: The Jews were originally polytheistic. The introduction to monotheism caused them to interpret their entire pantheon as different avatars of the the same entity. YHVH was originally derived from the Hewbrew god of war. Maaaaaybe something like that might be the case here? They just recognize other gods as being an extension of the one divine?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-19-2016, 06:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T14:02:23-08:00","id":1019412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1019008#post1019008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Also, just because the Abrahamic faiths doesn't give any power, doesn't mean the Titans don't. It was pretty obvious that the Titan of Light in 1st edition was supposed to be an allegory for the Abrahamic faiths by being the one and only being of worship, being too bright to look upon, and literally having angels serve him. Second edition might have another Titan who operates in the same fashion that was backing them throughout history.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was actually an in-universe reason for Aten having angelic minions that hd nothing to do with him being involved in the formation of Abrahamic religions. It was in fact post escape of the greater titans plot by Thoth to make said minions more predictable by tying them to a legend with a rigid structure. I thought it was an interesting way to showcase how a clever character could use fate binding in the setting and it kind of irks me when people just bush it off as a ham-fisted pot shot at monotheism.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T15:14:32-08:00","id":1019444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1019412#post1019412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There was actually an in-universe reason for Aten having angelic minions that hd nothing to do with him being involved in the formation of Abrahamic religions. It was in fact post escape of the greater titans plot by Thoth to make said minions more predictable by tying them to a legend with a rigid structure. I thought it was an interesting way to showcase how a clever character could use fate binding in the setting and it kind of irks me when people just bush it off as a ham-fisted pot shot at monotheism.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That sounds like it might have been extended material type of information. I own Hero, Demigod, and God and I don't recall reading that information anywhere. Unless I accidentally skipped over it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T15:31:46-08:00","id":1019455,"title":"","content":"It was in God, in the Titans section under &quot;lesser creatures of Akhenaten (p. 290, I had to look it up -_-).&quot; Vonpenguin's description of what Thoth was attempting is accurate. Which doesn't mean that Aten wasn't trying to manipulate/capitalize on the trappings of monotheism.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","user":"yukikaze","date":". 12-19-2016, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T18:49:50-08:00","id":1019550,"title":"","content":"Just because they don't have a Pantheon to make Scions, doesn't mean certain practitioners of the Abrahamic faiths can't wield divine powers. The 2E setting is a mythological sandbox and if there are sorcerers of the pagan faiths working magic independent of Scions, then it's very probable that the Abrahamic faiths can have miracle workers as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T15:00:39-08:00","id":1019991,"title":"","content":"Not to mnetion your averag person on the street doesn't know about the suprenatual. Governments know, though probably not as much as they'd like. But most mortals are in the dark.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T16:25:16-08:00","id":1020039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1019110#post1019110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Neal has already said that he likes that idea/explanation and that while Aten won't be solely responsible for the idea of monotheism, he will have played a large part in it. I think there was something said about him being responsible for exclusionary monotheism, though that confuses me since all monotheism is exlcusionary.</div> </div> </div> </div>In comparative religion, &quot;Monotheism&quot; refers to the belief in a supreme deity who is unique in power, but not in existence. Nobody in the world believes in only one deity-level supernatural entity. Christianity, for instance, has a spectrum of power from God Almighty through Satan, the Virgin Mary (at least for Catholics and Orthodox; not so much for Protestants), and various grades of saints and angels. (Not even bringing in the subtleties of Trinitarian doctrine.) Plenty of other mythologies and religions -- the Afro-Caribbean faiths, for instance -- posit a Supreme Deity as well; but in many of them, the Supreme Deity just sits around being Supreme while the subordinate deities do the interesting stuff and receive the active worship (because they might actually do something for you).<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T16:43:42-08:00","id":1020055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DShomshak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1020039#post1020039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In comparative religion, &quot;Monotheism&quot; refers to the belief in a supreme deity who is unique in power, but not in existence. Nobody in the world believes in only one deity-level supernatural entity. Christianity, for instance, has a spectrum of power from God Almighty through Satan, the Virgin Mary (at least for Catholics and Orthodox; not so much for Protestants), and various grades of saints and angels. (Not even bringing in the subtleties of Trinitarian doctrine.) Plenty of other mythologies and religions -- the Afro-Caribbean faiths, for instance -- posit a Supreme Deity as well; but in many of them, the Supreme Deity just sits around being Supreme while the subordinate deities do the interesting stuff and receive the active worship (because they might actually do something for you).<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak</div> </div> </div> </div>Those figures aren't recognized as lesser deities in the christian mythos. Satan isn't a godly figure, he's a fallen angel. In the bible, Angels are servants and warriors of God, not figures of worship. And the Saints are just people capable of performing miracles. They can channel God's power, but they aren't recognized as gods themselves. And the Virgin Mary was just a normal woman who was chosen to give birth to Jesus. She may be seen as a figure of great importance, but there's nothing inherently divine about her.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't know what Trinitarian is, but if it's anything like Father, Son and Holy Ghost, then you should know that all three of those are supposed to be the same person. Jesus is both the son of God, and at the same time is God himself. He's his own father, if you can wrap your head around that without it exploding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T17:34:24-08:00","id":1020075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1020055#post1020055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know what Trinitarian is, but if it's anything like Father, Son and Holy Ghost, then you should know that all three of those are supposed to be the same person. Jesus is both the son of God, and at the same time is God himself. He's his own father, if you can wrap your head around that without it exploding.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea that the Trinity are all the same entity has not always been the case. I like studying heresy more than cannon, so I might be rusty, but I believe the Nicene Creed in the 4th century is the development of the idea of the Trinity being the same entity. There have most certainly been heretical movements who denied the Creed, such as the Arian Heresy that kicked off with the Vandals, and I <i>think</i> the Cathars, technically. <br /> <br /> But, yeah, there have been times, and currently are places where the Trinity are worshiped as divergent entities. You get it in the rural Andes IIRC where the local, rural Pre-Incan beliefs are melded with Christianity and you get Jesus as a Mountain Spirit, Mary as a Mountain Spirit, all hanging out with local pre-Christian Divinities. Bugs the church, but they've not been able to find a solution for several centuries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T09:33:25-08:00","id":1020440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1020075#post1020075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The idea that the Trinity are all the same entity has not always been the case. I like studying heresy more than cannon, so I might be rusty, but I believe the Nicene Creed in the 4th century is the development of the idea of the Trinity being the same entity. There have most certainly been heretical movements who denied the Creed, such as the Arian Heresy that kicked off with the Vandals, and I <i>think</i> the Cathars, technically.<br /> <br /> But, yeah, there have been times, and currently are places where the Trinity are worshiped as divergent entities. You get it in the rural Andes IIRC where the local, rural Pre-Incan beliefs are melded with Christianity and you get Jesus as a Mountain Spirit, Mary as a Mountain Spirit, all hanging out with local pre-Christian Divinities. Bugs the church, but they've not been able to find a solution for several centuries.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be just my own experience but from what I've seen the subject of a trinity has been viewed as and treated wildly differently depending on the sect/denomination. I grew up in one that did say that the trinity was all one but in practice each was worshiped very separately and each was treated separately. I've seen others that treat and talk about the trinity like it was mentioned above, all the same person and more like three aspects of a singular god not unlike Vishnu. And still others where the trinity isn't even a thing and Jesus is either a renamed Michael the arcangel or just god's son but not a god himself.<br /> <br /> The sheer breadth of beliefs and worship styles of the abrahamic religeons allows for a very large number of variation.<br /> <br /> I am not sure where this thread is going but to bring it all to the point, I can definitely see the abrahamic faith being represented in someway in Scion. Either as different variation of the pagan mystics or as outright Scions (there are legends of offspring of angels in some of the abrahamic beliefs). <br /> <br /> idk, I think there is a lot that an ST can pull from if they desired it in their game. I don't know how much representation it would get in the books though. The books definitely strike me as harking to the old-age mythologies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T23:33:53-08:00","id":1021175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1020440#post1020440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I grew up in one that did say that the trinity was all one but in practice each was worshiped very separately and each was treated separately. I've seen others that treat and talk about the trinity like it was mentioned above, all the same person and more like three aspects of a singular god not unlike Vishnu.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually how Monotheism started among the Jews. They used to worship multiple deities as separate individuals, but over time, they attributed the entire pantheon to being different avatars of a singular god who would eventually go onto become the YHVH we know from the old testament. The original Yahweh was the Hebrew God of War, which probably explains his passion for violence and blood sacrifices. This is probably how the idea of a single, all powerful being came into the picture. Their feats were probably the work of different gods and goddesses who got slapped with the same identity once monotheism became more prevalent.<br /> <br /> <br /> Interestingly enough, there is a group of antagonists in 1E who are trying to pull off this very concept, by fooling mortals into believing that there is only one true god, and that all other gods are merely avatars for them to act through. Scions are also portrayed as being saints, rather than possessing divine blood. The idea is that get enough people to believe in this concept, and eventually Fate will make it reality! IIRC, the group was unwittingly a Titan worshiping cult who had been lured into serving Akhetaten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-23-2016, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T15:02:07-08:00","id":1021408,"title":"","content":"One thing I'm anticipating about 2e is that it's going to have a much more flexible mythology framework. Yes, we're still going to have the Hero/Demigod/God \u201cspine\u201d with a pantheon of gods at the top, for the most part; but unlike 1e, it won't stop there. <b>Origin</b> will present priests, prophets, and sorcerers; scions themselves will have a variety of geneses, not merely literal children of gods; mythological beings will be a thing beyond being \u201cBirthrights\u201d for Scions; 1e's concept of \u201cGreater Titans\u201d is being stripped of its inherently antagonistic elements and expanded into the concept of Primordials, which can arguably serve as \u201cGodheads\u201d for the surprising number of pantheons that include such a concept. Not every \u201cpantheon\u201d (by which I mean mythological constructs) is going to use all of these elements; and you can get some very different results by picking and choosing which elements a given mythology emphasizes. <br /> <br /> The Abrahamic faiths should be able to fit within this expanded mythological structure quite well, albeit in a very unorthodox manner: the traditional \u201cspine\u201d I mentioned earlier is likely to be all but nonexistent (Orthodox Christianity allows for exactly one Scion, while Judaism and Islam don't even allow for that; though some \u201cspin-offs\u201d like Mormonism allow for something closer to the Scion concept), with just about everything being handled outside of that spine: priests and prophets, <i>possibly</i> a rare Chosen Scion or equivalent (see Sampson), angels as what 1e called Lesser Immortals (a term that I hope 2e abandoned it implies an inferiority that isn't necessarily there), and a \u201cGodhead\u201d Primordial heading it up. <br /> <br /> If 2e keeps the notion that Primordials transcend mythology (as evidenced by the mythology-specific Avatars each Greater Titan manifested in 1e), I <i>could</i> see a single Primordial serving as the \u201cGodhead\u201d for several monotheistic faiths, including the ancient Egyptian episode where Aten worship was elevated to exclusionary monotheism status. But I'd want to emphasize the Mantle system that allows one god (or in this case, one Avatar) to belong to multiple Pantheons, taking on a slightly different face in each; and I'd definitely want to emphasize the fact that Primordials aren't inherently evil the way 1e's Greater Titans were.<br /> <br /> As for the Order of Divine Glory: this, I'd like to see restricted to a Shard that's designed specifically to pit monotheistic faiths against Pantheons: in this Shard, the idea is that the Order's Fate-Binding has the potential to retroactively exclude the Pantheons from the World, something that the Pantheons obviously have every reason to want to prevent. But I'd <i>only</i> want it to a Shard: in the default setting, I'd prefer the supernatural backing for Abrahamic faiths to be henotheistic rather than monotheistic, even if the <b>Origins</b> level still speaks in monotheistic terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T16:35:26-08:00","id":1021434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1021408#post1021408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Abrahamic faiths should be able to fit within this expanded mythological structure quite well, albeit in a very unorthodox manner: the traditional \u201cspine\u201d I mentioned earlier is likely to be all but nonexistent (Orthodox Christianity allows for exactly one Scion, while Judaism and Islam don't even allow for that; though some \u201cspin-offs\u201d like Mormonism allow for something closer to the Scion concept), with just about everything being handled outside of that spine: priests and prophets, <i>possibly</i> a rare Chosen Scion or equivalent (see Sampson), angels as what 1e called Lesser Immortals (a term that I hope 2e abandoned it implies an inferiority that isn't necessarily there), and a \u201cGodhead\u201d Primordial heading it up.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Mormons believe that all humans have the capacity to become gods through the teachings of Joseph Smith, and would go onto to rule their own planets after being judged worthy. Thus, in the context of this universe, all humans would be considered Scions within the Mormon faith.<br /> <br /> I don't remember where, but I think it was stated that mortal belief will not have an impact on the supernatural's existence within 2E. But rather faith (and Fate) will respond to how the supernatural behave around mortals. If you act like a benevolent, loving deity, then mortals and Fate will perceive you as such. If you act like a vengeful tyrant, then likewise, you'll be perceived as such by the mortal community.<br /> <br /> If this is the case, then it means Scions, Gods, Titans, and whatever else are now personally responsible for how they're portrayed within their respective religions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T14:47:34-08:00","id":1021708,"title":"","content":"I suspect that there need to be some limits to that rule. The interaction between Fate and gods is a two-way street; or at least it should be: it both informed the god's actions and is informed by them. On the mortal (\u201cOrigins\u201d) end of things, I can why someone without Legend would be unable to influence Fate; but unless they've been caught up in a Fatebinding, they ought to be able to exercise free will and think whatever they want of the gods. Which can lead to dissonance between what a good is actually like and how people perceive him.<br /> <br /> Under that model, though, the Order of Divine Glory doesn't work. Which is fine by me; all the more reason to consign then to a Shard where the rules get tweaked to allow them to work, instead of having them as part of the official setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T00:28:45-08:00","id":1025021,"title":"","content":"I know very little of Scion other than the basics, but to me many of the legendary figures in the bible seem like the kind of people you play in this game. Parting an entire ocean, calling down multiple scourges and disasters upon countries, wrecking mighty walls with music and a man strong enough to knock off pillars of a temple.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, Abrahamitic sects practically have a pantheon of its own with its angels that all seem to have different tasks and purviews, such as St. Michael who is a protector and warrior and St. Gabriel that delivers messages and inspires prophets. The hundreds of saints are also basically lesser gods, depending on how far you are willing to take this angle.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T06:19:45-08:00","id":1025061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1025021#post1025021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know very little of Scion other than the basics, but to me many of the legendary figures in the bible seem like the kind of people you play in this game. Parting an entire ocean, calling down multiple scourges and disasters upon countries, wrecking mighty walls with music and a man strong enough to knock off pillars of a temple.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, Abrahamitic sects practically have a pantheon of its own with its angels that all seem to have different tasks and purviews, such as St. Michael who is a protector and warrior and St. Gabriel that delivers messages and inspires prophets. The hundreds of saints are also basically lesser gods, depending on how far you are willing to take this angle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, most Scions make a habit out of not doing that stuff so openly in public. They don't want to get caught up in some Fatebond that might prove detrimental to them, and every time you use your powers in public, there's always the risk of establishing one.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd describe the Angels as being closer to Titans / Titanspawns. Unlike humans, they didn't have the privilege of free will. And they were the physical embodiment of various concepts, such as justice, hope, mercy, wisdom and death. When an Angel showed any attempt to defy God or think for themselves... well, they fell from grace. This either resulted in them transforming into demons, or in some more modern depictions, becoming humans as their wings were severed / plucked.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the saints and prophets, again, their power is not their own. Their bodies are a conduit through which they can channel God's power. Basically, God is using them as a tool through which to work his miracles on earth. Christ is the only one recognized as God's offspring in the Bible, and even that's confusing because some iterations claim that Christ is also God himself. Which makes Jesus less of a Scion and more of an avatar.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not saying that monotheism can't recognize the existence of other deities, while only worshiping one of them (plenty of cults do this). I'm saying that the Abrahamic faiths openly state that there is only <i>one true God</i> (theirs) and that all others are false idols. In the Scion setting, they would have to be strictly antagonistic because of this doctrine. I envision them as organizing into rallies, mobs and other hate groups to protest supernatural actions, as well as the men and women who would so brazenly call themselves the children of gods. Especially gods from different faiths, who their holy books decry as being false and blasphemous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-01-2017, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T19:56:59-08:00","id":1025247,"title":"","content":"I'm going to borrow some from one of my writers in this statement, but here goes: monotheism exists in <b>Scion</b>, and many, many people believe in one supreme omniscient, omnipotent God. Several schools of thought reconcile the mythic Gods with the God of Abraham, the Absolute, Mahavairocana, and the Supreme Being\u2019s other names. The Gods blanch at these things and mutter embarrassing anecdotes, when they deign to acknowledge these things at all.<br /> <br /> Scion is ultimately a game of mythology, though, and the setting must reflect that. Monotheism, as a belief in the World, is extremely useful as a culture jammer for intrapantheon rivalries, for denying another pantheon worship and Legend, as long-term transformational tools. Some of the organized religions in the World are more henotheistic than they are in our world. I consider the game to be sufficiently modular that if you want to exclude monotheism from the game, you can do so. Fundamentally, I'm uninterested in portraying anyone of sincerely-held faith in <b>Scion </b>as a dupe or an idiot. I'm also fundamentally uninterested in portraying the Gods as anything less than fully divine embodiments of the World - in other words, I want readers to see them as <i>gods</i>, not &quot;sufficiently powerful beings&quot;, even as player characters ultimately interact with them as mythic heroes do: people first, and not entities of worship. And yes, if we do the Elohim and Alihah Pantheons, there will be a King of the Gods, a son of his (the God of Samaria and Judah), and a certain powerful Sky God who all <i>glower</i> at each other.<br /> <br /> It's consumed an inordinate amount of bandwidth, but ultimately, no god worthy of the title proclaims themselves a god. It is self-evident. To quote Solas from Dragon Age, &quot;No real god need prove himself. Anyone who tries is mad or lying.&quot; To quote Zelazny in Lord of Light, &quot;Those who look upon gods then say, without even knowing their names, 'He is Fire. She is Dance. He is Destruction. She is Love.' So, to reply to your statement, they do not call themselves gods. Everyone else does, though, everyone who beholds them.&quot;<br /> <br /> (I should reiterate at some point that in terms of belief I am actually Roman Catholic, from the specifically Irish-American transmission. I studied theology in college and seriously considered the priesthood at one point. My confirmation saint was St. Jude Thaddeus, and I pray a novena to ask his intercession every evening.)<br /> <br /> Despite the considerable thought people have put into all these positions, most mortals don\u2019t bother with it. Millions of Christians in <i>our </i>world go to church on Sundays, and burn offerings at home, or in cult temples on other days, and don\u2019t see any contradictions. Same with the Orisha and the Loa. <b>Scion</b>'s World is even stranger. Never underestimate a person's capacity to quell cognitive dissonance. Cultural tradition sends you to one to get married and buried, and to the other for money, favors, or revenge. You have purists, intellectuals and eccentrics who do it differently, but in the World, most people simply sense an order of things, and act accordingly.<br /> <br /> I fully expect the Order of the Divine Glory and a Thronos Pantheon (under them arrayed the cherubim and the seraphim) to make an appearance once we get our community agreements up and running. I'm absolutely fine with that, and I really look forward to reading them. <b>Scion</b> and the World are big enough to support them all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 01-01-2017, 10:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T06:38:54-08:00","id":1025408,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all of that, Neall! I think that does a pretty good job of addressing most of the problems people have had with the issue of Monotheism in the game.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt does make perfect sense to think that henotheism is more of a thing in a setting like Scion, so I like that a lot. I love that you're not going to portray every Jew, Christian and Muslim as a dupe, the way 1e did. Definitely loving he idea of portraying the gods as their actual belief systems depict them.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd seriously? PLEASE make the Elohim and Aliha Pantheons at some point! Your description of what they'll be like sounds hilarious! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T08:05:33-08:00","id":1025439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1025247#post1025247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Scion is ultimately a game of mythology, though, and the setting must reflect that. Monotheism, as a belief in the World, is extremely useful as a culture jammer for intrapantheon rivalries, for denying another pantheon worship and Legend, as long-term transformational tools. Some of the organized religions in the World are more henotheistic than they are in our world. I consider the game to be sufficiently modular that if you want to exclude monotheism from the game, you can do so. Fundamentally, I'm uninterested in portraying anyone of sincerely-held faith in <b>Scion </b>as a dupe or an idiot. I'm also fundamentally uninterested in portraying the Gods as anything less than fully divine embodiments of the World - in other words, I want readers to see them as <i>gods</i>, not &quot;sufficiently powerful beings&quot;, even as player characters ultimately interact with them as mythic heroes do: people first, and not entities of worship. And yes, if we do the Elohim and Alihah Pantheons, there will be a King of the Gods, a son of his (the God of Samaria and Judah), and a certain powerful Sky God who all <i>glower</i> at each other.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>There is nothing about this paragraph that does not make me happy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T16:32:09-08:00","id":1025620,"title":"","content":"Possibly relevant here: According to Middle Eastern tradition, there are Jewish, Christian and Muslim jinn (as well as some who remain infidel). So there's precedent in mythology for supernatural creatures to follow the God of Abraham. It isn't just a mortal thing. (In fact, the Koran explicitly says the Prophet was sent to preach to both humans and jinn.)<br /> <br /> Personally, I always found the fretting over Scion and monotheism rather overblown.<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T22:18:32-08:00","id":1025735,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't see how this is a major problem. Just because Zeus or Thor are blatantly running in the World and God isn't doesn't mean that a member of the Abrahamic religions would have to admit to the former being gods. Someone could easily consider them to not be on account of some moral, spiritual, or defintional consideration. It might not make sense, but faith doesn't necessary have to in the first place, so why make a big deal about it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1675,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","user":"Weirdboyz","date":". 01-03-2017, 01:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T11:03:03-08:00","id":1026053,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I guess in this case the First Commandment is still pretty important, what with the &quot;Thou shall not have any Gods before Me&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T12:13:47-08:00","id":1026104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1026053#post1026053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I guess in this case the First Commandment is still pretty important, what with the &quot;Thou shall not have any Gods before Me&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYep. It always seemed odd to me that it was phrased like that. That automatically shows that Judaism was henotheistic at the time. Monotheism would say &quot;There ARE no other gods than me. Worship me exclusively.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200b&quot;Thou shalt not have any Gods before Me&quot; pretty much says &quot;There are other gods. It's even okay to show them some respect. But I'm the God you worship first and foremost.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T13:37:43-08:00","id":1026142,"title":"","content":"Well the Commandments originate from the Book of Genesis, which IIRC had lines implying that there were proxy wars going on between the Egyptian gods and the Abrahamic one. Such as the two Egyptian court priests transforming their staves into snakes, but Moses's sticksnake ate them. So yeah, in that part it was &quot;There are Gods, but I am YOUR God, worship me&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T02:58:58-07:00","id":1065152,"title":"","content":"My personal head canon is that the Titan Logos represents the Abrahamic God. The gods are wary over the Abrahamic faiths but nothing major appear to be made by the titan, both directly and indirectly, just the actions of fanatics both between each part of the faith and at those out of it. Aten then tries to usurp the worship of Logos by trying to look and act the part even making up angels loyal to him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6163-yama951","name":"Yama951","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T11:53:32-07:00","id":1065342,"title":"","content":"I tend to not let the whole &quot;Oh look, The Old Gods are real!&quot; impact my world by making sure that the governments and the churches actively suppress it. The governments do it because, if the general public knew that there were deities and they had divine powers, then why go to work? Just go to church and hope that your deity feeds you. The churches do it since they are not wanting it to get out that they could be wrong. These others are just the devil in disguise.<br /> <br /> That is not to mention Fatebinding issues that can occur.<br /> <br /> Now, I may alter my Scion world in 2e depending on how much flavor I get from the writers and how much setting info there is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T12:28:35-07:00","id":1065362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1026104#post1026104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bYep. It always seemed odd to me that it was phrased like that. That automatically shows that Judaism was henotheistic at the time. Monotheism would say &quot;There ARE no other gods than me. Worship me exclusively.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200b&quot;Thou shalt not have any Gods before Me&quot; pretty much says &quot;There are other gods. It's even okay to show them some respect. But I'm the God you worship first and foremost.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>EDIT: </b>Forgot I already mentioned this.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Strangely enough, the Hebrews were originally polytheistic, but gradually changed to monotheism and claimed the members of their pantheon were different avatars for the same being. Which clarifies why YHVH's behavior seems to contradict itself at times. It may have actually been a different avatar he was operating under at the time the story took place.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> On another note, that whole &quot;thou shalt not have any Gods before Me&quot; kind of brings up a question about Neall's assessment on what makes somebody a God. Since he quoted two characters who claim a true god doesn't refer to themselves as such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-20-2017, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T13:05:44-07:00","id":1065378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1065342#post1065342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The governments do it because, if the general public knew that there were deities and they had divine powers, then why go to work? Just go to church and hope that your deity feeds you.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;God helps those who help themselves.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T13:15:52-07:00","id":1065382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1065378#post1065378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;God helps those who help themselves.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;If you're helping yourself, what do you need God for?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Contrary to popular belief, religion is not a relationship between mortal and divine. It is, at the heart of it, a business transaction. We offer the Gods our sacrifices and worship, and they in turn provide us with tangible blessings.<br /> <br /> We wanted a good harvest, so we prayed for fertile lands and fair weather.<br /> <br /> We wanted to punish our enemies, so we prayed for justice and vengeance.<br /> <br /> We wanted to expand, so we prayed for strength and courage.<br /> <br /> We wanted knowledge, so we prayed for wisdom and clarity.<br /> <br /> And so on, and so on. If the Gods failed / refused to supply us with such things, then we would go off in search of one who was more pliable to our wishes. Nobody worships a God simply for being a God (unless they're brainwashed into it). They worship a God because they can make satisfying their needs and desires easier than they could under their own power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T13:38:12-07:00","id":1065401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1065362#post1065362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On another note, that whole &quot;thou shalt not have any Gods before Me&quot; kind of brings up a question about Neall's assessment on what makes somebody a God. Since he quoted two characters who claim a true god doesn't refer to themselves as such.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're taking Neall's quotes too literally...Gods refer to themselves as Gods all the time. Those two quotes seem to be indicating (to me at least) that Gods in the Scion verse don't <i>need</i> to declare their Divinity...no one looks upon a God and doesn't know bone deep that this is something Divine...like, say, the episode in the Aenied where Apollo appears in the form of Butes to Ascanius and the other besieged Trojans...everyone knows that this is a God...similarly, in the Mahabharata, when Krishna reveals his Divine Self to the members of an unbelieving court, even the blind king can see his Divinity. They just...know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T13:40:52-07:00","id":1065405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1065382#post1065382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;If you're helping yourself, what do you need God for?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Contrary to popular belief, religion is not a relationship between mortal and divine. It is, at the heart of it, a business transaction. We offer the Gods our sacrifices and worship, and they in turn provide us with tangible blessings.<br /> <br /> We wanted a good harvest, so we prayed for fertile lands and fair weather.<br /> <br /> We wanted to punish our enemies, so we prayed for justice and vengeance.<br /> <br /> We wanted to expand, so we prayed for strength and courage.<br /> <br /> We wanted knowledge, so we prayed for wisdom and clarity.<br /> <br /> And so on, and so on. If the Gods failed / refused to supply us with such things, then we would go off in search of one who was more pliable to our wishes. Nobody worships a God simply for being a God (unless they're brainwashed into it). They worship a God because they can make satisfying their needs and desires easier than they could under their own power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I so totally disagree with that in every way, shape, or form. The ancients worshiped the Gods because a God has the power to <i>destroy you, your family, and everything you hold dear. </i>Maybe without even realizing they did it. We offer sacrifice to the Gods in hope that they might notice us and spare us their inimitable wrath, and perhaps like us enough to offer something good as well. It has never been an equal relationship. In some canons (Babylonian stands out) mankind are created to be slaves of the Gods. Yes, it is true that you may seek the grace of other Gods to help because you don't like your original God and you want protection, but those Gods are going to require you to serve them instead. It's very much a relationship with an extreme power dynamic.<br /> <br /> I personally believe in God because, again, <i>in my personal views</i>, God represents the Eternal Truth of Reality, so I don't expect him to help me do everything for me because reality is and has never been easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T14:32:34-07:00","id":1065428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1065405#post1065405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I so totally disagree with that in every way, shape, or form. The ancients worshiped the Gods because a God has the power to <i>destroy you, your family, and everything you hold dear. </i>Maybe without even realizing they did it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not every God was depicted as being so callously destructive. Indeed, there are those who are considered to be quite benevolent and caring towards their worshipers. And unless you're monotheistic and believe in a singular, omnipotent being, then such gods couldn't afford to just smite everybody on a whim, because doing so would draw them into conflict with rival deities who may have been relying on the people they just destroyed in order to support their power.<br /> <br /> That's the great thing about polytheism; you have options! If there's a God you feel is abusing you or failing to live up to your expectations, you can find someone else to replace them.<br /> <br /> <br /> And praying to such gods in the hopes of not being destroyed still makes it a business transaction. &quot;I work for you, and you, in turn, spare my livelihood.&quot; There are many cases where people have lost faith in their gods, or even openly denounced them once their lives turns south. Their Gods weren't offering them protection anymore, so they saw no reason to remain subservient to them and instead turned towards other options to sustain themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T16:55:05-07:00","id":1065496,"title":"","content":"I think you're positing a universal or objective experience of polytheism that doesn't really exist. Also flanderizing apotropaic religion.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Well, darn, you're both doing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 03-20-2017, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T18:12:08-07:00","id":1065528,"title":"","content":"Humanity invented gods to answer questions they couldn't answer for themselves (&quot;where did I/we come from?&quot; &quot;What happens when we die?&quot; &quot;What makes rain?&quot; &quot;Why is there evil?&quot;), and to provide a reason to go on in the face of tragedy (&quot;if I build a home, plant crops, raise a family, and it can all be wiped out by a random mudslide, why bother? Oh, because the god of mudslides didn't get his sacrifice this moon cycle. If I just worship a bit harder, and make sure my neighbor does the same, we'll be blessed and spared.&quot;). The more we understand about the natural world (weather, eclipses, earthquakes, seizures, the life cycle of species, and so on), the more the worship has become spiritual instead of explanatory. Now, most see gods as shepherds of an afterlife, not direct bringers of plagues and storms. Of course, in a world where Chaac really <i>does </i>bring rain on those who piss him off, it changes perspectives a little bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T19:15:04-07:00","id":1065545,"title":"","content":"You're talking about etiology, which is something religion can and often does do, but is not the sum total of it. Etiological explanations of things aren't really in some kind of fundamental oppositional relationship with a scientific understanding of the world. You can do both. People do all the time.<br /> <br /> Like, it's not as if Christians and people of other religions are caught between this rock and a hard place where they can either say &quot;God did it.&quot; or &quot;you got me atheists, it was Thermodynamics, not God.&quot;<br /> <br /> How does heat rise? Thermodynamics. How does that happen? God made the world, and thermodynamics are a part of it.<br /> <br /> I posit that a world where lightning happens because Chaac wills it is not actually different from a world where it just happens (electrostatic discharge is still occuring either way!). The cause may change but what happens is still the same. Not a bad way to think about the World, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T20:09:54-07:00","id":1065561,"title":"","content":"The difference being, for game purposes anyway, is that in our world, we know it's basic electrostatic discharge in clouds, and in Scion, we know it's at least partly due to tangible, corporeal beings called Gods (or storm nymphs, or dragons, or whatever you choose). How you see the real world doesn't really enter into a game about myths. Not saying anyone is wrong in their worldview - just saying the game is about the beings of myth in a magical world, one where religious views are different from our own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T23:07:38-07:00","id":1065600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1065561#post1065561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference being, for game purposes anyway, is that in our world, we know it's basic electrostatic discharge in clouds, and in Scion, we know it's at least partly due to tangible, corporeal beings called Gods (or storm nymphs, or dragons, or whatever you choose).</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that, by all accounts, it could very well be tangible, corporeal beings called Gods (or storm nymphs, or dragons, or whatever you choose) in real life that control electrostatic discharge in clouds, and we just don't know it because we are but mere mortals. I think the argument that is happening here, really, comes down to whether or not you think the conceit of Scion is &quot;like our world, but the Gods are real&quot; or &quot;the world is the same, but all religions are equally true, and you're chosen by a God so you interact with them regularly.&quot;<br /> <br /> Both are valid arguments, but it's obviously gonna make people snippy whenever religion starts getting questioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T00:34:33-07:00","id":1065613,"title":"","content":"The mythical creatures of the world tend to avoid humanity when possible... and when it isn't... most humans will tend to see what they expect. While a true believer in the Tuatha may see fairies frolicking in a park... or even one of the Aes Sidhe running a business... most others will tend to dismiss such things or see them as something else entirely (because they don't expect it). Even so, there tends to be few places in mortal society for such beings... thus they retreat to the wild places and terra incognita that humans avoid or just don't know about.<br /> <br /> \u200bMany places that have haunted reputations and are avoided by people tend to be homes for such creatures. A few may even make deals with settlements, such as a water sprite/nymph blessing the spring that feeds a town with water with healing properties in exchange for one virgin a year to come to her and satisfy her (and sometimes being kept)... or have the water turned to poison.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs for how Abrahamic religions could come to have a greater influence on a world where old gods exist... the same methods they used in our world would likely work... incorporating the &quot;pagan&quot; customs and celebrations into their religion would make it easier to convert those who's gods rarely answer prayers anymore. This would likely be far more effective than purges, witch hunts or crusades which tend to cause populations to hide their true faith (and even if one converts under torture, one likely returns to their true faith when no one is looking).<br /> <br /> \u200bIn the end, while it is likely that Christianity and other Abrahamic faiths still did much of what they did in our world, the results would have been less effective... with people continuing their &quot;pagan&quot; rituals in private... at least the ones that weren't adopted by these new faiths. Many old gods also likely got new names as Saints, Angels or other celestial beings in these religions... and offering one's prayers to Zeus's new identity as a Saint still sends the power of that worship to Zeus... while maintaining the illusion of being faithful to Christianity.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn the end, like much of the Scion world... faith, worship and the Gods are a matter of perception... something that is very fluid in this setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T08:31:44-07:00","id":1065786,"title":"","content":"I guess the thing that always gets me is this; we have a cool game called Scion. In it, the gods of myth and legend are real. You can play the chosen of such beings, and do great deeds that change the course of lives, rivers, and history. Magic is real. Faeries, centaurs, dragons, and other amazing beings are real. Odin, Re, Tezcatlipoca, Amaterasu, Athena - and hundreds of other such beings - are real, and interact with people. The opportunities for fantastic games are endless. So why is it necessary to try to drag it down to/ground it in a world where the real-world faiths are so important, complete with every-day bigotry, conflict, contradiction, and a decided dearth of the interactive deities and larger-than-life heroes and heroines that are the whole point of the game in the first place? Why not just play something else that deals with real-life religions and involves as many guardian angels and house spirits as you are comfortable using? Ever since 2nd edition was announced, there have been calls of &quot;how can I play a mortal?&quot;, and &quot;how do we spotlight christianity?&quot; Don't. If you want to do those things, play something designed around mortals, like Fate, or GURPS, or even basic CoD, then just make it as religiously-grounded as you want. The beauty of Scion, the reason most of us got into it in the first place, wasn't &quot;oh, hey, look, a game where I can play a priest of God&quot;, but &quot;Wow - a game where I can <i>play</i> a god, and mingle with figures of myth.&quot; And I think that's the coolest thing about the game; that you can play as the superheroes of legend. If I play Champions, or DC Adventures, I don't play the sidekicks and cabbies, or the cannon fodder agents. I play the hero (or maybe the villain). And for me, that's Scion, but with gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T08:56:16-07:00","id":1065807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1065786#post1065786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the thing that always gets me is this; we have a cool game called Scion. In it, the gods of myth and legend are real. You can play the chosen of such beings, and do great deeds that change the course of lives, rivers, and history. Magic is real. Faeries, centaurs, dragons, and other amazing beings are real. Odin, Re, Tezcatlipoca, Amaterasu, Athena - and hundreds of other such beings - are real, and interact with people. The opportunities for fantastic games are endless. So why is it necessary to try to drag it down to/ground it in a world where the real-world faiths are so important, complete with every-day bigotry, conflict, contradiction, and a decided dearth of the interactive deities and larger-than-life heroes and heroines that are the whole point of the game in the first place? Why not just play something else that deals with real-life religions and involves as many guardian angels and house spirits as you are comfortable using? Ever since 2nd edition was announced, there have been calls of &quot;how can I play a mortal?&quot;, and &quot;how do we spotlight christianity?&quot; Don't. If you want to do those things, play something designed around mortals, like Fate, or GURPS, or even basic CoD, then just make it as religiously-grounded as you want. The beauty of Scion, the reason most of us got into it in the first place, wasn't &quot;oh, hey, look, a game where I can play a priest of God&quot;, but &quot;Wow - a game where I can <i>play</i> a god, and mingle with figures of myth.&quot; And I think that's the coolest thing about the game; that you can play as the superheroes of legend. If I play Champions, or DC Adventures, I don't play the sidekicks and cabbies, or the cannon fodder agents. I play the hero (or maybe the villain). And for me, that's Scion, but with gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is fine, but given that there have been lots of calls of &quot;how can I play a mortal?&quot; and &quot;how do we spotlight Christianity?&quot; it's pretty clear that there are <i>lots </i>of people who feel that this was <i>missing </i>from Scion 1st ed. Some people like to play awesome sidekicks and cabbies, and cannon fodder agents, because these are <i>people </i>and people matter. Also, given that Hinduism is present in the game and devotees of Kali or Vishnu can enjoy playing an agent of their IRL God or Goddess, some Christians may like the idea of being empowered by Archangel Michael or perhaps serving Jesus Christ as a heroic Saint.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's that detrimental of a desire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T11:52:10-07:00","id":1065877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1065807#post1065807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is fine, but given that there have been lots of calls of &quot;how can I play a mortal?&quot; and &quot;how do we spotlight Christianity?&quot; it's pretty clear that there are <i>lots </i>of people who feel that this was <i>missing </i>from Scion 1st ed. Some people like to play awesome sidekicks and cabbies, and cannon fodder agents, because these are <i>people </i>and people matter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Props to those who try to play Samwise. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T12:11:53-07:00","id":1065882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1065877#post1065877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Props to those who try to play Samwise. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Tolkien always said he was the true hero, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T17:27:47-07:00","id":1066059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1065496#post1065496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also flanderizing apotropaic religion.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://tse1.mm.bing.net/th?id=OIP.CcH3uA92t493lS4xqL5gKgEsES&amp;pid=15.1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <span style=\"font-size:48px\">\u200bStupid Flanders!</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T17:35:56-07:00","id":1066063,"title":"","content":"Stupid sexy Cernunnos...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T18:17:03-07:00","id":1066080,"title":"","content":"You can play a devotee of Vishnu, or a priest of Jesus, in any RPG out there; all you need to do is say that's what you are playing; with the right GM, you can even run an entire campaign centered around Christianity or Islam or any other faith. You can also play a cabbie or cop in a super-hero universe without ever needing the heroes (and if you are playing a Batman/Daredevil style, you never need powers at all even if you play the heroes), if that's what you want to play. But for me, Scion is about <i>playing the Scions that eventually become gods, </i>not the pizza delivery guy or the Buddhist nun who get caught in things. You <i>can</i> play them, but it escapes me why you want to buy a game designed to be about mythical gods, just so you can play mundane people or Abrahamic followers. But YMMV, certainly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T20:58:20-07:00","id":1066112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1066080#post1066080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and if you are playing a Batman/Daredevil style, you never need powers at all even if you play the heroes</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Batman doesn't have any powers (<i>if you don't count being able to catch machine gun fire with his hands; yes that's a thing he did</i>). He's just a multi billionaire with access to military grade technology, is a master of over 20 different forms of martial arts, has the body of an Olympic athlete and received training in psychology, investigation and escape artistry from some of the greatest masters in the world. He is, in short, the absolute pinnacle of human achievement; something which the vast majority of mortals will never come close to.<br /> <br /> <br /> Daredevil has senses that are so acute, they basically function at the level of sonar. So saying he doesn't have any powers is not quite accurate when he has 360 degree 'vision' in and out of combat.<br /> <br /> <br /> In fact, most of the heroes and villains in popular media who 'don't have powers' do have access to something the rest of us don't: Wealth and connections, often to ridiculous levels!<br /> <br /> Joe, the pizza guy isn't going to have access to a quiver full of trick arrows, contacts with foreign powers, or the physical conditioning of a Green Beret. Which is why Scion isn't about playing an average mortal (unless you want a comedic setting, like Powerless.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-22-2017, 12:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T21:20:58-07:00","id":1066117,"title":"","content":"Because comic books, like most adventure fiction [and mythology!], are based around larger-than-life characters. Why? Because it's not likely that a comic about Joe, the pizza guy, would reach a wide market among super-hero comic readers [readers of indie comics are a different thing, of course. They might love it!]. His stories wouldn't have the same level of drama and mythological adventure, and if they did, then you aren't really playing &quot;mortal Joe, the pizza guy&quot; anymore. And a game about the same pizza guy wouldn't require a game like Scion to simulate it; you would probably be better off using something more grounded in &quot;reality&quot;. It would also be a completely different type of story than the adventures of the Scions of five Gods/Goddesses who are drawn together to prevent disaster and change the world itself.<br /> <br /> My point is, you don't need Scion-type rules to simulate this, if that's what you want to play. There's nothing wrong with playing it, if that's what you like - different strokes and all that. But why ask if we can get Scion-level rules for playing said pizza guy, or a mundane worshiper of some real-world religion? That's not what the game is supposed to be about, because it's being designed to enable players to take the roles of mythical Scions. And it's about the great religions of the past, and the myths and legends surrounding their Gods and Goddesses [and Scions, monsters, wizards, and others] - if this is the game you want to play, then the Abrahamic faiths should most probably be no more important than the other faiths, and possibly even less so. And if you want to play with angels, saints, and the real-world gods, that's an entirely different theme, and maybe Scion isn't the best foil for what you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T04:45:43-07:00","id":1066238,"title":"","content":"The intrinsic association of Christianity and &quot;playing mortals&quot; in this thread is bizarre and makes no sense. These are not the same things and tying them together at the baseline just seems to make for repetitive statements about &quot;What Scion Is&quot; that seem to access something adjacent to the point of the game. <br /> <br /> Let's not mistake permission for obligation. A system like Storypath facilitates a tacit &quot;permission&quot; to play characters of interesting means and backgrounds like Batman or a Druid who grew up in the woods or a wolf-man via Paths. That does not mean that picking &quot;regular pizza boy&quot; is somehow athematic or a consequence of someone making a mistake in choosing to play Scion, and that's a completely facile position to take.<br /> <br /> You can play the pizza guy. He can have power or whatever. He can be Christian or whatever. Neall said as much. No one of these traits inherently invalidates the others and there is no dichotomy there. It isn't athematic to do so because &quot;themes&quot; are not this straight jacket of behavior they're being made out to be.<br /> <br /> Essentializing these traits seems like an unecessary and unsophisticated privation of concepts.<br /> <br /> Also &quot;and the real world gods&quot; is not the best wording for this conversation, FYI.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T05:18:45-07:00","id":1066243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1066238#post1066238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The intrinsic association of Christianity and &quot;playing mortals&quot; in this thread is bizarre and makes no sense. These are not the same things and tying them together at the baseline just seems to make for repetitive statements about &quot;What Scion Is&quot; that seem to access something adjacent to the point of the game.<br /> <br /> Let's not mistake permission for obligation. A system like Storypath facilitates a tacit &quot;permission&quot; to play characters of interesting means and backgrounds like Batman or a Druid who grew up in the woods or a wolf-man via Paths. That does not mean that picking &quot;regular pizza boy&quot; is somehow athematic or a consequence of someone making a mistake in choosing to play Scion, and that's a completely facile position to take.<br /> <br /> You can play the pizza guy. He can have power or whatever. He can be Christian or whatever. Neall said as much. No one of these traits inherently invalidates the others and there is no dichotomy there. It isn't athematic to do so because &quot;themes&quot; are not this straight jacket of behavior they're being made out to be.<br /> <br /> Essentializing these traits seems like an unecessary and unsophisticated privation of concepts.<br /> <br /> Also &quot;and the real world gods&quot; is not the best wording for this conversation, FYI.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Not saying playing a regular mortal is anathemic, just pointing out that they really aren't going to be capable of doing anything significant in the Scion universe, especially if the mythical creatures and what-not are actively / passively hiding their existence. At that point, it's no longer a game about mythical creatures and grand quests, it's just a slice of life story told from the perspective of people who have no idea what's going on.<br /> <br /> <br /> I mentioned earlier that there's a new comedic series set in the DC universe called <b>Powerless</b>, which focuses a bunch of ordinary civilians who live in a world with super powered individuals and how they deal with that realization. They don't have gadgets, they don't have special training, they don't fight crime when nobody's looking. They're just your average, every day officer workers who have to deal with the occasional alien invasion or whatever. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T05:47:15-07:00","id":1066257,"title":"","content":"That being mortal means they can't do anything significant does not actually follow at all and is exactly what I'm talking about. Like, seriously think about that for a second.<br /> <br /> Similarly, the idea that pizza boy or Christian just magically transfigures the game into &quot;slice of life where people have no idea what's going on&quot; is really loaded and another example of exactly what I'm talking about. These assumptions plain don't need to be made, and the dictation of what follows from them can detract from people's ability to understand the flexibility of the game and the world.<br /> <br /> It's a very prescriptive way of talking about the game, and I don't think you're giving Scion it's due by suggesting everything outside of this framework you're coming up with has to be comedy or &quot;slice of life told from the perspective of people who have no idea what's going on.&quot;<br /> <br /> Another Onyx Path game, Exalted can have this problem too. People often say stuff like &quot;people that aren't Exalted don't matter.&quot; And well... Have you ever looked outside? Yknow, at this entire planet full of people? Are you really going to have none of them matter or ever do anything in your games because they aren't Scions? It's fun to imagine some people from history as Scions, too, right? But do you think EVERY major historical figure was one? The answers to those questions don't really matter for the purposes of this discussion, but the point is kind of that regular people DO matter in the World. Not because you need some big objective statement in-universe about them mattering, but because they're people.<br /> <br /> Who are your characters friends? Foes? Lovers? Rivals? Not all of them will be gnomes or pixies or satyrs and not all of them will be Scions either. Sometimes conflicts with people are more complicated than just just beating each other up.<br /> <br /> This isn't some kind of &quot;Humanity, fuck yeah!&quot; post but rather a reminder that regular people actually do matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T06:20:05-07:00","id":1066271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1066257#post1066257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That being mortal means they can't do anything significant does not actually follow at all and is exactly what I'm talking about. Like, seriously think about that for a second.<br /> <br /> Similarly, the idea that pizza boy or Christian just magically transfigures the game into &quot;slice of life where people have no idea what's going on&quot; is really loaded and another example of exactly what I'm talking about. These assumptions plain don't need to be made, and the dictation of what follows from them can detract from people's ability to understand the flexibility of the game and the world.<br /> <br /> It's a very prescriptive way of talking about the game, and I don't think you're giving Scion it's due by suggesting everything outside of this framework you're coming up with has to be comedy or &quot;slice of life told from the perspective of people who have no idea what's going on.&quot;<br /> <br /> Another Onyx Path game, Exalted can have this problem too. People often say stuff like &quot;people that aren't Exalted don't matter.&quot; And well... Have you ever looked outside? Yknow, at this entire planet full of people? Are you really going to have none of them matter or ever do anything in your games because they aren't Scions? It's fun to imagine some people from history as Scions, too, right? But do you think EVERY major historical figure was one? The answers to those questions don't really matter for the purposes of this discussion, but the point is kind of that regular people DO matter in the World. Not because you need some big objective statement in-universe about them mattering, but because they're people.<br /> <br /> Who are your characters friends? Foes? Lovers? Rivals? Not all of them will be gnomes or pixies or satyrs and not all of them will be Scions either. Sometimes conflicts with people are more complicated than just just beating each other up.<br /> <br /> This isn't some kind of &quot;Humanity, fuck yeah!&quot; post but rather a reminder that regular people actually do matter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> When I say they aren't able to contribute anything of significance, I'm talking about their capabilities when compared to the mythical creatures. It's pretty much agreed upon that mortals stop posing a direct threat after you start getting into Demigod territory. Ordinary mortals are used as followers, which quickly becomes downgraded to canon fodder and expendables as the game progresses (I've seen several people claim that combat followers are worthless). Sure, a mortal who trains their body on a constant basis over the course of many years might be able to lift a few hundred pounds over their head, but that's not really impressive when a brand new Scion instantly gains the ability to lift weights exceeding 500 lbs. and quickly escalates to several tons as they continue to train themselves. And no matter how great at marksmanship you may be, you're probably going to need anti-aircraft weaponry to take down somebody that can break the sound barrier in their jogging shoes. And even a silver tongue and years of experience in the political arena falls flat once you encounter beings who can hypnotize others with a glance, or radiate the sex appeal of a forest nymph!<br /> <br /> <br /> Anything a mortal can do, they can do a hundred times better. Which means that anything a mortal does is going to pale in comparison to their accomplishments.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In order for the average mortal to contribute anything of importance, the game would have to be either A) set in the Hero / Origin power level when the enemies are weak and inexperienced, or B) they'd have to be working as a pawn for a more powerful entity around Demigod / God level.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I really don't understand how you can claim otherwise. These are ordinary men, women and children getting involved in the affairs of gods, titans and monsters. If they're not being manipulated into service, or taking on basic rookies, then chances are they're either going to die horribly, or they're Legendary in some fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-22-2017, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T09:11:00-07:00","id":1066356,"title":"","content":"Well, to begin with, I never said &quot;ordinary people don't matter&quot;. They can, and do, save lives, change history, start wars, end wars, explore space, study science, invent religions, and do many many other valuable things. But Scion [which is what this whole discussion is about] wasn't designed to be about them. It's a game about the chosen of the Gods, people who are born from or gifted by beings like Athena or Amaterasu. You can play an entire campaign around Joe the pizza guy and his friends; you could probably make it pretty cool with a god GM and players. And you could make it as faith-based as you wanted it to be. But you wouldn't need Scion rules to do it. Why would you deliberately buy a game about the Scions of the Gods, and then say, &quot;but it doesn't let me play mortals&quot;? If you want mortals, there are plenty of games on the market that let you play them, some of them very good games. Scion probably isn't the best choice for such a tale.<br /> <br /> Including the Abrahamic faiths also opens up another can of worms; how do you stat God/Allah? If you do, then he's just another god among many, and the prominence of his worship doesn't make sense <i>in the context of Scion. </i>And if you hand-wave him, with a &quot;Psht, he's God, he can do anything&quot;, then that reduces all the other gods to lesser status, which kind of negates &quot;all myths are true&quot; as a core concept. By the concept of the game, and the fact that it is an RPG, the existence of the Abrahamic God is problematic at best, game-wrecking at worst.<br /> <br /> As I've said before, this is an RPG, not a text on real-world faiths. People did, and do, worship the so-called &quot;pagan&quot; religions, so they are far from invalid forms of spiritual belief. I use the term &quot;real world gods&quot; to differentiate between the deities of the real world we live in, and the ones in the game of Scion - I'm not sure how that is a problem for anyone. This is a discussion [civil, I hope] about a game, not a debate on theism.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T09:24:18-07:00","id":1066366,"title":"","content":"You stat God / Allah the same way you stat all the other pantheon chiefs in the game. Yvhv isn't the only deity to claim they built the universe, you know? Nor is he the only deity who claims to be perfect in all things. So if all myths are true, then fine, he can claim to have created everything that exists. Just as any other pantheon can do the same! Yvhv is a Legend 12 deity with Avatar levels Purviews as far as the gameplay mechanics are concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T09:56:15-07:00","id":1066402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1066356#post1066356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I use the term &quot;real world gods&quot; to differentiate between the deities of the real world we live in, and the ones in the game of Scion - I'm not sure how that is a problem for anyone. This is a discussion [civil, I hope] about a game, not a debate on theism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that Vishnu is a &quot;real world god.&quot; Kali is a &quot;real world god.&quot; There are millions of people who genuinely worship these deities today in the real world. If you include neopagans, there are people out there who actually genuinely worship Zeus, Hera, Dionysus, and Horus, Ra, Isis, etc. The Gods in Scion are <i>real world gods. </i>They are not D&amp;D Gods, definitely fake and made up by folks at TSR or Wizards of the Coast. The Gods in Scion <i>are real. </i>And whether you are theist or atheist personally, <i>there are lots and lots of people throughout history who have worshipped these Gods and still </i><b>do</b>.<br /> <br /> So why is it any more of a stretch to put <i>Jesus Christ </i>- also a <i>real world God</i> - or his father YHWH into the game? Why is it so weird to want to play a game where you are doing incredible, mythical things in the name of your God? Hindu people - <i>in the real world </i>- are playing Scions of their personal God, and doing things in their name. Why is it weird for Christians to want the same? That's what I don't understand. The only way that I can imagine it is that you, on some level, view Jesus Christ or YHWH as being &quot;more real&quot; than Vishnu, which is sort of a slap in the face to millions of Hindus who view Krishna as the supreme godhead.<br /> <br /> Scion is a game about service to the Gods, and heroism. Asking &quot;where does <i>my</i> God fit into this setting?&quot; is not athematic.<br /> <br /> As for playing mortals in the setting, Odysseus is a mortal. He never becomes a God. His cunning and intelligence helps him outsmart mythical creatures and survive the wrath of a full-blown deity. Yes, he has the <i>help </i>of the Gods, but nobody is saying that a mortal character can't have the help of the Gods in their quest. When I, at least, ask &quot;can I play a mortal/priest of a god&quot; I am asking if I can play, say, Odysseus. And I feel that setting up Odysseus as being &quot;more than human&quot; is disingenuous, since his humanity - his desire for mortality and a happy life at home with his beloved wife and son, even when offered immortality and divinity - is central to his story.<br /> <br /> ...I have a lot of strong feelings about this subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T10:17:19-07:00","id":1066427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1066402#post1066402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that Vishnu is a &quot;real world god.&quot; Kali is a &quot;real world god.&quot; There are millions of people who genuinely worship these deities today in the real world. If you include neopagans, there are people out there who actually genuinely worship Zeus, Hera, Dionysus, and Horus, Ra, Isis, etc. The Gods in Scion are <i>real world gods. </i>They are not D&amp;D Gods, definitely fake and made up by folks at TSR or Wizards of the Coast. The Gods in Scion <i>are real. </i>And whether you are theist or atheist personally, <i>there are lots and lots of people throughout history who have worshipped these Gods and still </i><b>do</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe there is a slight misunderstanding about what Purple Snit means by 'Real World Gods' and I wanted to weigh into the conversation to help with the possible confusion. As a game, Scion has to make some compromises in different situations to represent different Deities. Some situations are inherently too theologically complex to weave into a game line that has any semblance of balance, therefore the Gods in Scion are not purely the 'Real World Gods.'<br /> <br /> For example, a Deva, Theoi, Teotl, and Dia are all fundamentally different beings. Different cultures have different conceptions of what a Deity 'is' fundamentally. A Dia (Irish) is a being that is very, very capable of dying. A being that exists at a finominal level of power, but is dwarfed by many other Pantheons. Theoi are truely immortal, and a Dia is not. The Deva are hugely, cosmically powerful, while a Dia is very much not.<br /> <br /> However, for the sake of balance, all of these Pantheons are equalized effectively. All Gods are Gods, and that is something that is not true in the real world. Deities from one culture to another are fundamentally different, sometimes to a massive degree. Everyone who is Legend 12, be they Lugh or Vishnu, are roughly batting at the same level, and that is very much a construction of Scion as a game.<br /> <br /> So, I believe that is what Purple Snit was discussing with dividing Scion-Gods and Real-World-Gods. The Gods in Scion are beings inspired maybe 99% (probably more like 85%) from the real world, but the actual nitty gritty details can't be properly represented in the game if it is going to be balanced. (I have tried, and brainstormed ways to divine up the Pantheons more for accuracy, but it just breaks down. The big thing is the Dia and Deva exist on opposite ends of a power spectrum which just would not contribute to a fun environment for players)<br /> <br /> Purple Snit is also probably addressing the ideas that we get in the Scion Books of Gods limelighting as mortals sometimes, which, depending on the Pantheon, a God may never, ever, ever do. But, for the sake of the game, a compromise is made with the original 'Real World God' to fiddle with the cannonical truth of the Deity to make it work within Scion. Same with how Scion goes, &quot;Er, sure, okay, the Irish Pantheon is kicking around and not (almost) all dead.&quot; just little deviations from the cannonical truth of the real world to make the game work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T10:27:05-07:00","id":1066434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1066427#post1066427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, for the sake of balance, all of these Pantheons are equalized effectively. All Gods are Gods, and that is something that is not true in the real world. Deities from one culture to another are fundamentally different, sometimes to a massive degree. Everyone who is Legend 12, be they Lugh or Vishnu, are roughly batting at the same level, and that is very much a construction of Scion as a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair, and I can get behind that. But I feel like if we are compromising for the sake of story, then I see no reason that the Abrahamic God cannot be the same. He is a God, a powerful, Legend 12 God. He is not the all powerful, omnipotent God that he is within the &quot;real life worship&quot; of Christianity, but he is a God, and he is real. He got the drop on the Egyptians one time and hasn't let them forget it since. He really, really, really hates the Canaanite Gods, like a whole lot. Why is his worship so prominent? Because a lot of people worship him. Why didn't the other Gods try and stop him? They <i>did try. </i>Christians faced a <i>shit ton </i>of persecution for their beliefs in the Roman empire, and the Jews are<i> still</i> getting killed right and left. The only way that Christianity ultimately solidified was by adopting traits of other pantheons' worship within their own. And I think that is sort of what Neall is going for in this edition, anyhow.<br /> <br /> Claiming that we can't compromise with the Christian God the way Scion has already done for Krishna the Supreme Godhead is just extremely weird to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T11:17:59-07:00","id":1066480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1066356#post1066356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, to begin with, I never said &quot;ordinary people don't matter&quot;. They can, and do, save lives, change history, start wars, end wars, explore space, study science, invent religions, and do many many other valuable things. But Scion [which is what this whole discussion is about] wasn't designed to be about them. It's a game about the chosen of the Gods, people who are born from or gifted by beings like Athena or Amaterasu. You can play an entire campaign around Joe the pizza guy and his friends; you could probably make it pretty cool with a god GM and players. And you could make it as faith-based as you wanted it to be. But you wouldn't need Scion rules to do it. Why would you deliberately buy a game about the Scions of the Gods, and then say, &quot;but it doesn't let me play mortals&quot;? If you want mortals, there are plenty of games on the market that let you play them, some of them very good games. Scion probably isn't the best choice for such a tale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's what I find funny about this whole argument, from both people who loudly wonder if Scion allows mortal play, and those who don't think that that is an ideal game mode...Origins is kind of exactly that...it allows a wide variety of player types that are not Scions, and most importantly, it's the book with the core ruleset...the core ruleset that is what you need to play a mortal game...You don't start a game book with descriptions of Powers, you start it with Attributes and Skills...the things you need to model the mortal world, because you can't go immortal without first establishing the mortal...so yes, of the four core books of Scion one is already designed specifically to allow non-Scion play, including mortals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1066356#post1066356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Including the Abrahamic faiths also opens up another can of worms; how do you stat God/Allah? If you do, then he's just another god among many, and the prominence of his worship doesn't make sense <i>in the context of Scion. </i>And if you hand-wave him, with a &quot;Psht, he's God, he can do anything&quot;, then that reduces all the other gods to lesser status, which kind of negates &quot;all myths are true&quot; as a core concept. By the concept of the game, and the fact that it is an RPG, the existence of the Abrahamic God is problematic at best, game-wrecking at worst.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, you could make him a Primordial...he's a vastly powerful distant being who interacts with the world directly rarely, usually sending down Intermediary Angels or Chosen Prophets, he seems like a textbook Primordial to me. And IIRC Danu is a Primordial who still occasionally chooses Scions so te Abrahamic God doing it isn't unprecedented. Also, while his worship is prominent all preview material seems to indicate that worship of other Pantheons never faded to the extent it did in ours, so you wouldn't have to try to justify his prominence...no more than you need to explain why Ameterasu hasn't booted the Buddha out of Japan (or Sarasvati for that matter). Godly worship spreads, sometimes more changed than others...Yama is working at least three jobs, after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1066356#post1066356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I've said before, this is an RPG, not a text on real-world faiths. People did, and do, worship the so-called &quot;pagan&quot; religions, so they are far from invalid forms of spiritual belief. I use the term &quot;real world gods&quot; to differentiate between the deities of the real world we live in, and the ones in the game of Scion - I'm not sure how that is a problem for anyone. This is a discussion [civil, I hope] about a game, not a debate on theism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand what you're trying to say by using the term 'real-world Gods' but here's why it is coming off as a problem...you are specifically saying that there is one real world God that doesn't translate to a God in the game of Scion, whereas all the others are fine, and for both worshipers of that God, and worshipers of other Gods that have been translated, that can come off as strange.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T15:42:26-07:00","id":1066603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1066366#post1066366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You stat God / Allah the same way you stat all the other pantheon chiefs in the game. Yvhv isn't the only deity to claim they built the universe, you know? Nor is he the only deity who claims to be perfect in all things. So if all myths are true, then fine, he can claim to have created everything that exists. Just as any other pantheon can do the same! Yvhv is a Legend 12 deity with Avatar levels Purviews as far as the gameplay mechanics are concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> More on the topic of statting him, we can take a look at the stories told about him to get an estimate of how he'd work mechanically. Epic <b>Wisdom</b> and <b>Charisma</b> are obvious, but what about physical attributes? To my knowledge, there aren't really any stories that depict the Abrahamic God of performing great feats of physical Strength and Dexterity. <b>Stamina</b> is a possibility, because of the whole Crucifixion thing.<br /> <br /> <b>As for his Purviews:</b> Health, Fertility, Sun, Animal, Guardian and Psychopomp would be the most iconic powers within his arsenal. Along with some less specialized talent in the Fire, Earth, Sky, Water, Justice, Death and Mystery.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, in short, Yhvh is a deity who focuses more on amassing Purviews than attributes, which fits into his theme of rarely showing himself in person and instead choosing to act through displays of power and proxy agents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-25-2017, 07:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T15:48:34-07:00","id":1066609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1066603#post1066603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Stamina</b> is a possibility, because of the whole Crucifixion thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, to be fair, even if you're statting Jesus as YHWH instead of his own deity (which I would do, as a Scion of YHWH who ascended to the Right Hand of the Father, even though that would make me an Arian heretic...compromise here) he does in fact suffer, bleed, and die as a result of the flogging and the crucifixion. He doesn't just take it like it's nothing. I mean, he comes back to life, but that sounds, again, like more of a miraculous purview than a sign of his incredible physical fortitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T15:58:37-07:00","id":1066612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1066609#post1066609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, to be fair, even if you're statting Jesus as YHWH instead of his own deity (which I would do, as a Scion of YHWH who ascended to the Right Hand of the Father, even though that would make me an Arian heretic...compromise here) he does in fact suffer, bleed, and die as a result of the flogging and the crucifixion. He doesn't just take it like it's nothing. I mean, he comes back to life, but that sounds, again, like more of a miraculous purview than a sign of his incredible physical fortitude.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Meh, it's a coin toss. Some Christians believe Jesus was an individual, and others (i.e Catholics, i.e half the Christian population) believe he was an avatar of God, himself.<br /> <br /> But as for him having epic Stamina, keep in mind that he was mercilessly whipped, had his limbs dislocated and was nailed to a cross by his wrists and feet, stabbed in the side with a spear, and bore a crown of thorns. All of this and it still took him 3 days on the cross before he finally died. That sounds like somebody who doesn't go down easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-22-2017, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T16:08:50-07:00","id":1066615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1018992-how-does-the-abrahamic-faiths-have-power-in-the-scion-world?p=1066612#post1066612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh, it's a coin toss. Some Christians believe Jesus was an individual, and others believe he was an avatar of God, himself.<br /> <br /> But as for him having epic Stamina, keep in mind that he was mercilessly whipped, nailed to a cross by his wrists and feet, stabbed in the side with a spear, and bore a crown of thorns. All of this and it still took him 3 days on the cross before he finally died. That sounds like somebody who doesn't go down easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, most modern Christians believe that Jesus was simultaneously an individual and an avatar of God and God himself all at once, and you shouldn't think about it too hard because it's a mystery known only to the Highest. That's how these things go. If I was &quot;compromising&quot; to fit into Scion's setting, which generally has &quot;pantheons,&quot; I'd make Jesus an individual God (or, at the very least, an individual patron, even if fluff-wise he is still God) in his own right just for the sake of playable variety.<br /> <br /> Also, it didn't take three days for him to die. He died after he got stabbed with the spear. It took him three days to come back to life.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't argue it too much, though. I'd just be happy to play a Saint in a Scion game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T16:27:45-07:00","id":1066622,"title":"","content":"The tale of him coming back to life 3 days later is well known, but I could have sworn it was also mentioned that he was on the cross of three days before succumbing to his injuries.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, while he was dead, he was apparently traveling around the Underworld, liberating the souls of the damned from other pantheons (such as the Greco-Roman). So one might say that the crucifixion marked the transition from Hero to Demigod, and his resurrection marked his apotheosis to Godhood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T18:05:29-07:00","id":1066650,"title":"","content":"I'll avoid debating the reality of deities in the real world we live in, because this is a thread about the game Scion, not a thread about theism. The difference I'm trying to establish, and I'll try one more time to make myself understood, is that we are talking about the myths/faiths of a version of Earth that exists in a role-playing game (not real-world faiths). I'm not talking about right-here-and-now Hinduism, Islam, Asatru, Wicca, or any other faith system (real-world faiths). I'm talking about a game with sets of numbers and abilities that represent mythical beings and their offspring that you can tell tales about and play. Nothing more. I'm not debating your personal beliefs, or mine. If someone wants to play Yhwh as a Legend 12 deity, and have him exist alongside Atum-re, Enki, Osiris, Marduk, al'Uzzah, and all the other deities of the Middle East, fill your boots, you certainly can. It's not something that interests me, which is also a legitimate viewpoint. I just get frustrated when people come to a game about subject X, and then grumble that they can't play an entirely different type of game with the rules presented to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}